          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kent.schwartz@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Mar 14 2024 17:10:01 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Basins can increase infection risk</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Using a basin to clean your incontinent patients may increase the risk of infection. Clinical studies have shown basins are often contaminated with bacteria, including multi-drug resistant organisms and gram-negative bacilli.<sup>1,2</sup> Hospital water systems have also been identified in more than 29 studies as the source of serious waterborne hospital-acquired infections (HAIs).<sup>3</sup></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Mar 14 2024 17:10:51 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
